# 4. MY LEARNING — THE CORE FEATURE

This is one of the most important parts of Dev Hub.

Members will often already be learning from external resources.

They might use:
- Udemy courses.
- YouTube courses and playlists.
- Downloaded courses.
- PDFs and personal notes.
- Official documentation.
- Online tutorials.
- Other educational resources.

**Members should NOT be required to upload their entire downloaded courses or course materials to Dev Hub.**

Dev Hub is not a course-hosting platform.

Instead, members should tell the platform what course or learning resource they are using.

### Adding a course

Allow members to:

- Enter the course name.
- Select the programming language or field.
- Paste a course or playlist URL, where available.
- Select the topics they are currently studying.
- Enter their current lesson or module.
- Add a short description of their course.
- Add their own learning resources or reference links.

For downloaded courses, members should be able to enter the course name and manually add the modules or topics they are following.

The platform should also support a custom learning path for members who use multiple resources.

### Understanding external courses

The AI can use accessible course information, publicly available descriptions, links, and member-provided topic information to help structure learning.

For YouTube resources, use accessible video information and transcripts or captions where available.

Never pretend to have watched or analyzed a video or course that the system cannot access.

If the AI needs more information, ask the member to provide the topic, lesson title or a short explanation of what they studied.

### Learning plan

Once a member adds their course, Dev Hub should organize their learning around:

- Learning stages.
- Modules.
- Topics.
- Daily learning targets.
- Practice exercises.
- Quizzes.
- Weekly projects.

The AI should compare their learning resource against their selected roadmap and identify important topics they might be missing.

The member should be able to follow their existing course without being forced to abandon it.

